prompts.brief:
TASK: write the creative brief that starts a new collection.

PRODUCT: {{product.full_name}}. {{product.brief_en}}
CLIENT THEME: {{input.short_description}}
WORKING TITLE (may be empty): {{input.title}}
TARGET AGE: {{input.target_age}} years
AGE PROFILE (binding rules): {{age_profile}}
CLIENT NOTES (may be empty): {{input.additional_comments}}
CLIENT'S STORY FOR VOLUME 1 (may be empty): {{input.seed_story}}
EARLIER REJECTED DIRECTIONS, DO NOT REPEAT THEM (may be empty): {{rejections}}

Write a creative brief that makes this collection feel top-tier, warm and original, never generic or "low budget".
Write "collection_title" and "logline" in {{input.language}} (reader-facing). Write every other field in {{ui_language}} (it is read by the editor).

Reply with ONLY this JSON object:
{"collection_title": "", "logline": "", "tone": "", "core_values": [""], "educational_goals": [""], "narrative_rules": [""], "visual_direction": "", "avoid": [""]}

prompts.series:
TASK: design the series arc of the collection.

CREATIVE BRIEF: {{brief}}
AGE PROFILE: {{age_profile}}
CLIENT THEME: {{input.short_description}}
CLIENT NOTES (may be empty): {{input.additional_comments}}
CLIENT'S STORY FOR VOLUME 1 (may be empty; if present, volume 1 IS this story and volumes 2-6 continue from it): {{input.seed_story}}

Design the arc of exactly {{structure.volumes}} volumes. Each volume is a complete, self-contained story that can be read alone; together they share the same characters and a gentle through-line that grows from volume to volume. Vary settings, situations, emotions AND the kind of ending across volumes (bedtime is not the default ending; give each volume an "ending_type" and avoid repeating the same one in consecutive volumes). Every volume must offer at least {{structure.pages}} visually distinct, drawable moments.

Titles in {{input.language}}; every other field in {{ui_language}}.
Reply with ONLY this JSON:
{"through_line": "", "volumes": [{"number": 1, "title": "", "summary": "", "learning_goal": "", "main_setting": "", "emotional_arc": "", "ending_type": ""}]}

prompts.critic:
TASK: EVALUATE THIS VOLUME SCRIPT as the publisher's senior editor, with fresh eyes. You see only the text and the rules, never the writer's intentions.

RUBRIC (score every criterion by its code): {{rubric}}
AGE PROFILE: {{age_profile}}
STORY BIBLE (names and looks must match): {{bible_volume.characters}}
REQUIRED PAGES: {{structure.pages}}. TEXT LENGTH GUIDELINE: about {{age_profile.max_chars}} characters per page. The age profile is guidance, not a hard rule: judge whether the text truly suits the age, not the exact count.
CAST PLAN FOR THIS VOLUME (who must appear, who returns and why): {{cast_volume}}

SCRIPT: {{script}}
AUTOMATIC WARNINGS FROM THE STRUCTURE CHECK (may be empty; verify them): {{warnings}}

Score EVERY rubric criterion 0-10 (10 = ready to print at a top publisher) and give, for each, one short quote from the script as evidence. List only concrete, fixable issues, each with its page (null only if it concerns the whole volume), the criterion code, the exact quote and a precise fix. Write in {{ui_language}}.
Reply with ONLY this JSON:
{"criteria": [{"code": "T01", "score": 0, "evidence": ""}], "strengths": [""], "issues": [{"page": 1, "code": "T01", "quote": "", "problem": "", "fix": ""}]}

prompts.revise:
TASK: Revise this volume script applying the editor's review. Keep everything that works, fix every listed issue, keep exactly {{structure.pages}} pages and exactly the same JSON schema.

AGE PROFILE: {{age_profile}}
STORY BIBLE: {{bible_volume}}

SCRIPT: {{script}}
EDITOR REVIEW: {{critique}}
Page text in {{input.language}}; scene fields in {{ui_language}}.
Reply with ONLY the full revised JSON.

prompts.notes:
Convert the reviewer's notes on a children's book collection into precise, actionable production constraints for the writers and illustrators. One constraint per item, imperative voice, in {{ui_language}}. Interpret vague notes in the spirit of the brief.

REVIEWER NOTES: {{notes}}
CREATIVE BRIEF: {{brief}}

Reply with ONLY this JSON: {"constraints": [""]}

prompts.polish:
TASK: final copy edit of volume {{n}} of {{structure.volumes}} of a premium children's picture book, before print.

AGE PROFILE (guidance, not a hard rule): {{age_profile}}
STORY BIBLE: {{bible_volume}}
CAST PLAN FOR THIS VOLUME: {{cast_volume}}
APPROVED SCRIPT: {{script}}
PRODUCTION CONSTRAINTS FROM THE REVIEW (must be honoured; may be empty): {{constraints}}

Polish every page's text for read-aloud rhythm, warmth and precision in {{input.language}}. Guideline: about {{age_profile.max_chars}} characters per page; it may vary by roughly a third when the story needs it. Keep every field of every page (purpose, actions, effects, final_locations, coloring_scene, objects, location, must_not_show, sound, educational, page_turn, continuity) and the architecture. Keep the story, exactly {{structure.pages}} pages, the scenes and the characters; change scene or composition only if a constraint requires it. Add a back-cover blurb (2-3 sentences in {{input.language}}) and the short labels printed on the covers, translated into {{input.language}}.

Reply with ONLY this JSON:
{"title": "", "cover": {"scene": "", "characters": [""], "setting": ""}, "pages": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "purpose": "", "scene": "", "actions": [{"character": "character-id", "action": "exactly what this character visibly does, using its allowed way of holding things"}], "coloring_scene": "", "characters": ["character-id"], "objects": ["object-id"], "location": "location-id", "must_not_show": [""], "effects": "none|natural: ...|fantasy: ...", "dialogue": "", "sound": "", "educational": "", "page_turn": "quiet", "composition": "", "text_zone": "bottom", "continuity": "", "final_locations": {"character-id": "only on the last page: where each character ends up"}}], "architecture": {"beginning": {"pages": "1-3", "summary": ""}, "development": {"pages": "4-6", "summary": ""}, "climax": {"pages": "7-9", "summary": ""}, "ending": {"pages": "10-12", "summary": ""}, "emotional_arc": "", "educational_intent": [""], "why_age_fit": ""}, "back_cover_blurb": "", "labels": {"volume": "Volume", "storybook": "Storybook", "coloring_book": "Coloring book", "title_page": "A story and colouring book", "rights": "All rights reserved.", "ai_notice": "Text and illustrations created with the help of artificial intelligence and reviewed by the publisher."}}

prompts.correct:
TASK: you are revising one artifact of a premium children's book production in response to reviewer feedback.

ARTIFACT: {{artifact_label}}
CURRENT JSON: {{current}}
REVIEWER FEEDBACK: {{feedback}}
ANCHORED COMMENTS ON THIS ARTIFACT (may be empty): {{comments}}
CONTEXT THAT MUST STAY CONSISTENT: age profile {{age_profile}}; reader language {{input.language}}; editor language {{ui_language}}.
STORY BIBLE (may be empty): {{bible}}

Apply the feedback precisely and change nothing else. Keep exactly the same JSON schema and the same number of items in every list. Reply with ONLY the full revised JSON.

prompts.cast:
TASK: plan the CAST (who appears in which volume) of a collection of {{structure.volumes}} volumes.

SERIES ARC: {{series}}
STORY BIBLE (characters with ids and roles): {{bible.characters}}
AGE PROFILE (guidance): {{age_profile}}

Plan who appears in which volume so the collection feels alive and connected:
- The ONE main character appears in every volume and leads each story.
- Secondary characters are introduced gradually (not all in volume 1), step back for one or more volumes, and RETURN later with a clear, satisfying reason (they help, they changed, they need help). Each returning character gets a small arc across the collection.
- Keep each volume's cast comfortable for the age (the profile's max_characters is a guideline for one volume).
- presence is one of: "introduced" (first appearance), "appears", "returns" (back after being absent), "mentioned" (only talked about), "absent".
Write purposes and arcs in {{ui_language}}.

Reply with ONLY this JSON:
{"main_character": "character-id", "characters": [{"id": "character-id", "role": "main", "arc": "", "volumes": [{"volume": 1, "presence": "introduced", "purpose": ""}]}], "notes": ""}

prompts.continuity:
TASK: CONTINUITY CHECK of the whole collection.

STORY BIBLE: {{bible.characters}}
CAST PLAN: {{cast}}
VOLUMES (compact: title, then per page the text, scene and characters): {{volumes_compact}}

1. Build a continuity ledger: for every character, per volume where they appear, what they did, what they learned and how their relationships changed.
2. List concrete continuity problems: wrong names or looks, a character present who should not be (or missing when the plan needs them), a returning character not re-introduced, contradictions between volumes, relationships that jump without reason. Only real problems, each with a precise fix.
Write in {{ui_language}}.

Reply with ONLY this JSON:
{"ledger": [{"id": "character-id", "volumes": [{"volume": 1, "did": "", "learned": "", "relationships": ""}]}], "issues": [{"volume": 1, "page": 3, "problem": "", "fix": ""}]}

prompts.continuity_fix:
TASK: Fix ONLY these continuity problems in this volume script, change nothing else, keep exactly {{structure.pages}} pages and the same JSON schema.

SCRIPT: {{script}}
CONTINUITY PROBLEMS TO FIX: {{issues}}
STORY BIBLE: {{bible_volume.characters}}
CAST PLAN FOR THIS VOLUME: {{cast_volume}}
Page text in {{input.language}}; scene fields in {{ui_language}}.
Reply with ONLY the full corrected JSON.

prompts.adapt:
TASK: as a native {{input.second_language}} children's author, ADAPT (do not translate word for word) volume {{n}} of a premium picture book from {{input.language}} into natural, idiomatic {{input.second_language}} that a native parent loves reading aloud.

SOURCE (approved final text): {{script}}
AGE PROFILE (guidance): {{age_profile}}
CHARACTER NAMES (never change): {{bible.characters|pluck:name}}
CLIENT'S OWN STORY FOR THIS VOLUME (may be empty; if it contains a {{input.second_language}} version, stay as close to it as the final source allows, only polishing): {{seed_story_for_volume}}

Rules:
- Same page count and the same event on each page ("n" stays linked to the source page); you may restructure sentences, reorder clauses and choose different words so it sounds native.
- No calques or literal constructions; prefer everyday words and natural word order; avoid stacked diminutives and redundant adjectives (e.g. for Romanian prefer "o băltoacă" or "o bălticică", never "o băltoacă mică"); natural onomatopoeia of {{input.second_language}}.
- Keep rhythm, warmth, refrains and the rule-of-three patterns, re-created in {{input.second_language}}.
- Remove any ambiguity (who does what, where each character sleeps).
- Similar length to the source; the age guideline applies.
In "notes" (in {{ui_language}}) list choices a human should double-check.
Reply with ONLY this JSON:
{"collection_title": "", "title": "", "pages": [{"n": 1, "text": ""}], "back_cover_blurb": "", "labels": {"volume": "", "storybook": "Storybook", "coloring_book": "Coloringbook", "title_page": "", "rights": "", "ai_notice": ""}, "notes": [""]}

prompts.native_critic:
TASK: NATIVE ADAPTATION REVIEW. Evaluate this {{input.second_language}} adaptation for a native parent reading aloud.

AGE PROFILE: {{age_profile}}
ORIGINAL ({{input.language}}): {{source}}

ADAPTATION: {{script}}
AUTOMATIC ALIGNMENT WARNINGS FROM THE PAGE-BY-PAGE CHECK (may be empty; verify them first): {{warnings}}

Check: sounds natural and idiomatic (no word-for-word calques), no awkward or redundant phrasing, grammar and diacritics, read-aloud rhythm, no ambiguity (who does what, where each character sleeps), same events as the original page by page, age-appropriate words. Score 0-10. List only concrete problems with a better wording. Write in {{ui_language}}.
Reply with ONLY this JSON: {"score": 0, "strengths": [""], "issues": [{"page": 1, "problem": "", "fix": ""}]}

prompts.native_revise:
TASK: Revise this adaptation applying the editor's review; keep everything that works, keep exactly {{structure.pages}} pages and the same JSON schema.

ADAPTATION: {{script}}
EDITOR REVIEW: {{critique}}
ORIGINAL: {{source}}
Reply with ONLY the full revised JSON.

prompts.page_fix:
TASK: revising SPECIFIC PAGES of volume {{n}} of a premium children's picture book, exactly as the publisher asked.

FULL VOLUME (context; keep continuity with the neighbouring pages): {{current}}
PAGES TO CHANGE (page number, the publisher's request; "rewrite": true means the page was rejected and must be written again from scratch in a clearly better way): {{requests}}
AGE PROFILE (guidance): {{age_profile}}
Text language: {{lang}}. Keep names, facts, the cast plan and the flow of the story. Change ONLY the listed pages.
Reply with ONLY this JSON: {"pages": [ {the complete revised page object for each listed page, same fields as in the volume, including "n"} ]}

prompts.revise_pages:
TASK: REVISE ONLY THESE PAGES of a volume script, applying the editor's issues. Every other page stays exactly as it is.

AGE PROFILE: {{age_profile}}
STORY BIBLE: {{bible_volume}}

FULL VOLUME (context; keep continuity with the neighbouring pages): {{script}}
ISSUES TO FIX (page, criterion code, quote, problem, fix): {{issues}}
Page text in {{input.language}}; scene fields in {{ui_language}}. Keep names, facts, the cast plan and the flow of the story.
Reply with ONLY this JSON: {"pages": [ {the complete revised page object for each page listed in the issues, same fields as in the volume, including "n"} ]}

prompts.continuity_inc:
TASK: CONTINUITY CHECK of a new volume against the approved continuity ledger.

STORY BIBLE: {{bible.characters}}
CAST PLAN: {{cast}}
CONTINUITY LEDGER OF THE VOLUMES BEFORE (approved; the source of truth for what already happened): {{previous_ledger}}

NEW VOLUME(S) TO CHECK (compact: title, then per page the text, scene and characters): {{volumes_compact}}

1. Return the continuity ledger entries of the NEW volume(s) only (the app keeps the entries above): for every character who appears, what they did, learned and how their relationships changed.
2. List concrete continuity problems of the NEW volume(s) only: wrong names or looks, a character present who should not be (or missing when the plan needs them), a returning character not re-introduced, contradictions with the ledger, relationships that jump without reason. Only real problems, each with a precise fix.
Write in {{ui_language}}.

Reply with ONLY this JSON:
{"ledger": [{"id": "character-id", "volumes": [{"volume": 1, "did": "", "learned": "", "relationships": ""}]}], "issues": [{"volume": 1, "page": 3, "problem": "", "fix": ""}]}

prompts.retro:
TASK: volume retrospective. Read everything that happened to ONE finished volume and extract what the team should learn.

TEAM AGENTS (use these ids): {{agents}}
RUBRIC CODES: {{codes}}
EXISTING LESSONS (id, agent, code, text): {{existing}}

VOLUME: {{volume_label}}
PUBLISHER'S DECISIONS AND NOTES AT THE GATES: {{decisions}}
EDITOR'S ISSUES (by criterion): {{critic_issues}}
VISUAL CHECK PROBLEMS AND REDRAWS: {{visual}}
MANUAL EDITS BY THE PUBLISHER: {{edits}}

Look for PATTERNS (the same kind of problem on several pages or at several gates), not single incidents. A lesson is a short imperative rule in Romanian, useful for future volumes; give it the criterion code it improves.
Reply with ONLY this JSON: {"worked": [""], "repeated_problems": [{"code": "T01", "pages": [1], "summary": ""}], "confirm": ["existing lesson id"], "new_lessons": [{"agent": "", "code": "T01", "text": ""}]}
